--
N5008 [namespace.udecl]/3, [class.inhctor.init]/1: `using base::base;' in a
class template names the constructors of its dependent base class (here
through a member typedef, as libstdc++ writes it); they are inherited, and
`translator<T, I, C>(t)' is initialized by base's constructor.  The front
end finds no constructor ("found no match for symbol 'translator'"), drops
the constructor of the enclosing matcher and verifies a wrong result.  The
same happens with the base named directly (`using translator_base<T, I,
C>::translator_base;') and for direct construction.  This is libstdc++'s
regex `_RegexTranslator' (`using _Base::_Base;'), used by _AnyMatcher,
_CharMatcher and _BracketMatcher (regex_compiler.h:352/373/410/434, 5
cbmc-cpp regex descs in the round-163 audit).  Header-free reduction.
Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
